{"E:\\videos\\olc02\\wt\\vlog\\olc02\\voz\\b006_t3.wav": {"text": "Lars, my second cook, used to put a shake of hot sauce on top and call it a Swedish breakfast for supper. What does it cost today? About two dollars and sixty cents for the whole skillet, four plates, that's 65 cents a plate, cover first, brown after. And you know what I noticed that first night? Nobody asked where the meat was. A hot skillet of potatoes with the eggs still soft on top, a cup of coffee, and the crew went quiet the way a crew only goes quiet when the food is good. That's when I knew we'd get through those two weeks. Supper number two, cabbage and noodles. The Polish boys in the crew called it holuski, and the first time I made it, Big Swede looked at the pot and said, that's it, cabbage? Then he had three plates, one head of green cabbage, two onions, 6 tablespoons of butter or half butter and half bacon fat, 12 ounces of white egg noodles,", "words": [{"w": " Lars,", "s": 0.08, "e": 0.4}, {"w": " my", "s": 0.4, "e": 0.66}, {"w": " second", "s": 0.66, "e": 1.1}, {"w": " cook,", "s": 1.1, "e": 1.88}, {"w": " used", "s": 1.88, "e": 1.96}, {"w": " to", "s": 1.96, "e": 2.14}, {"w": " put", "s": 2.14, "e": 2.3}, {"w": " a", "s": 2.3, "e": 2.46}, {"w": " shake", "s": 2.46, "e": 2.72}, {"w": " of", "s": 2.72, "e": 2.92}, {"w": " hot", "s": 2.92, "e": 3.16}, {"w": " sauce", "s": 3.16, "e": 3.46}, {"w": " on", "s": 3.46, "e": 3.74}, {"w": " top", "s": 3.74, "e": 4.12}, {"w": " and", "s": 4.12, "e": 4.46}, {"w": " call", "s": 4.46, "e": 4.8}, {"w": " it", "s": 4.8, "e": 4.92}, {"w": " a", "s": 4.92, "e": 5.02}, {"w": " Swedish", "s": 5.02, "e": 5.4}, {"w": " breakfast", "s": 5.4, "e": 5.92}, {"w": " for", "s": 5.92, "e": 6.22}, {"w": " supper.", "s": 6.1, "e": 6.88}, {"w": " What", "s": 6.88, "e": 7.28}, {"w": " does", "s": 7.28, "e": 7.54}, {"w": " it", "s": 7.54, "e": 7.66}, {"w": " cost", "s": 7.66, "e": 8.0}, {"w": " today?", "s": 8.0, "e": 8.9}, {"w": " About", "s": 8.9, "e": 9.2}, {"w": "